#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:5
#: c4f8ff7f065348b793ad8c4a464470ae
msgid "Vibration Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:7
#: 56e6ea15ed444c8898789a6a24bbeaea
msgid "The vibration failsafe is a little different than most other failsafes in ArduPilot, in that it does not initiate a flight mode change. Instead it changes the algorithm which controls altitude and climb rate in altitude control modes. It is enabled by default, but can be disabled by setting :ref:`FS_VIBE_ENABLE<FS_VIBE_ENABLE>` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:10
#: 80c6bb28ca2e45fea1c370a6a4b79e5d
msgid "Impact of High Vibrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:12
#: e8ea690804c04b67b608c6d6b83fa53e
msgid "Multicopters can suffer from very high vibration levels (more than 60m/s/s) which can lead to the accelerometers saturating (i.e. going beyond the range that the sensor can measure). This leads to “clipping” and means the EKF cannot accurately calculate its climb rate or vertical acceleration. This can lead to the vehicle becoming unable to control its climb rate and, in severe situations, can lead to the vehicle climbing rapidly at full throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:15
#: 3d66a715a96c4c1ab41cf946a2d211ea
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:17
#: b99be9c4d4c34c43b5fd996a67fe39e9
msgid "The vibration failsafe will trigger if all of the following are true for at least one second:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:19
#: cc346f80f5fd42dfa1723780278710e2
msgid "EKF’s vertical velocity innovations are positive (see onboard log's XKF3.IVD value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:20
#: 31911ee8803b4742b8fd3e3f001b98ad
msgid "EKF's vertical position innovations are positive (see XKF3.IPD)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:21
#: f8f5f297daa749358befe0c130e78447
msgid "EKF's velocity variance is 1 or higher (see XKF4.SV)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:23
#: e70757424160489c99c0b203e98f0f3d
msgid "An ``Innovation`` is the difference between the predicted value and the latest (non-IMU) value. A ``Variance`` is the EKF’s reported confidence in its estimate. 0 is very good, >1 is bad."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:26
#: 98fb8587073e403ba5f9988cdd4bf803
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:28
#: 47d6b85f9c84442497858ccfed87c5a3
msgid "If the vibration failsafe triggers the following will happen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:30
#: c2ded7572f194877a4b89b2b0e0ccb77
msgid "“Vibration compensation ON” will appear on the Ground Stations HUD. EKF’s climb rate will be calculated using a 3rd order complementary filter which is tuned to be more resistant to vibration (but less accurate) than the normal method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:31
#: ca17430af80843eabcf5d2c04e17a1a8
msgid "Altitude controller switches to a more vibration resistant two-stage controller (position->velocity) instead of the regular three-stage controller (i.e. position->velocity->acceleration)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:32
#: 2377bb2ef03a4085a20eb08fd953b5be
msgid "The vehicle will not change mode but its altitude hold will be less accurate than normal. The vehicle may overshoot it’s altitude targets and/or respond more slowly to pilot input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:35
#: 604ebbef543740dab7f0d5265e1cd5b6
msgid "Recovery from the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:37
#: 2b0ae0295c2a41e3bc1b3cc533314fb9
msgid "Vibration failsafe will deactivate 15 seconds after the EKF returns to normal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:38
#: 375d300b2fb34b41a54003c9db7a5c1f
msgid "“Vibration compensation OFF” will be displayed on the HUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/vibration-failsafe.rst:39
#: e9c77c67fb454625acfb6d57c34f88b4
msgid "Altitude and climb rate controllers will return to their normal methods"
msgstr ""
